{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline","id":1541727,"title":"[V20] Is Abyss Mysticism, mechanically speaking, a seperate Discipline?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-08T03:49:32-07:00","id":1541727,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V20] Is Abyss Mysticism, mechanically speaking, a seperate Discipline?","content":"My major point of confusion arises from this section:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rites of the Blood, Page 37</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Abyssal Rituals</b><br /> The following rituals do not adhere to the same rules as<br /> other forms of magic, in large part because they build on a<br /> Discipline that is not truly a form of sorcery. <b><i>To learn Abyss<br /> Mysticism, a Cainite must have at least one dot in both<br /> Obtenebration and one dot in Occult.</i></b> Such a character may<br /> not learn Abyss rituals rated higher than her<i> <b>Obtenebration<br /> or Occult score (whichever is lower)</b></i>. Casting Abyss rituals<br /> requires a successful Wits + Occult roll, for which the<br /> difficulty equals 3 + the level of the ritual (maximum 9). Only<br /> one success is required for a ritual to succeed. Should a roll<br /> to activate an Abyss ritual fail, the Storyteller is encouraged<br /> to create particularly horrible consequences or side effects;<br /> the Abyss demands a heavy penance for failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>And<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lore of the Clans, Page 126</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Abyss Mysticism is difficult and time consuming to learn,<br /> and comes at a cost. Its rituals often have side effects that create<br /> Flaws the character cannot remove that provide no bonus<br /> points. <b><i>To learn the power, a vampire must have at least one<br /> dot in both Obtenebration and Occult.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>The Limitation reads to me as if Obten (Or Occult) should be treated as the Thaum Score, however, it constantly being referred to as a seperate Power and all that kinda gives me the impression like you can buy it if you have obten+occult.<br /> <br /> Edit: If one could point me to sources about this that are somewhat more clear on the matter, I would appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T05:14:38-07:00","id":1541730,"title":"","content":"It's just clumsy writing. Abyss Mysticism rituals are just rituals attached to Obtenebration, with an additional (somewhat silly) prerequisite in Occult rating. The weirdo language is a vestige from earlier editions, when Necromancy/Mortis weren't treated as blood sorcery but still had rituals.<br /> <br /> Now, DAV20 <i>does</i> have optional rules for treating Abyss Mysticism as a form of blood sorcery proper, and in that case the Obtenebration discipline acts as primary path. But, that's a consequence of how DAV20 treats blood sorcery as a single unified discipline, with all proprietary forms just acting as &quot;paradigms&quot; so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-08-2024, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T07:03:30-07:00","id":1541734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline?p=1541730#post1541730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just clumsy writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline?p=1541730#post1541730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyss Mysticism rituals are just rituals attached to Obtenebration, with an additional (somewhat silly) prerequisite in Occult rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all the flak that V5 gets, making Blood Sorcery and Oblivion single disciplines and the rest as rituals/ceremonies, was a good idea. Simplifies a lot of path / magic style inflation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T08:15:43-07:00","id":1541738,"title":"","content":"It was a good idea to mesh similar Disciplines together in V5 in my eyes and to me that is always a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T10:35:20-07:00","id":1541742,"title":"","content":"Abyss Mysticism &quot;rituals&quot; are actually a weird blend between ritual and amalgam powers, so to speak. They're pretty unique.<br /> <br /> For V20, looking at the actual rituals dismisses a lot of the doubts, they're basically powers that you buy at a fixed XP cost and have Obtenebration + Occult as prerequisites.<br /> <br /> V5 doesn't really gives you the same vibe as the original Abyss Mysticism, but that's neither good or bad. Abyss Mysticism was really weird, so not always the best mechanic for what it was supposed to represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T14:47:42-07:00","id":1541750,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Mysticism isn't a Discipline even if it's weird in every edition.<br /> <br /> Can we not turn yet another thread into a V20 vs V5 debate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T07:41:10-07:00","id":1541779,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the responses! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Learning something new everyday and getting closer to figuring out the language that is being used, lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28457-xasure","name":"Xasure","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T16:43:21-07:00","id":1541817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline?p=1541742#post1541742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyss Mysticism &quot;rituals&quot; are actually a weird blend between ritual and amalgam powers, so to speak. They're pretty unique.<br /> <br /> For V20, looking at the actual rituals dismisses a lot of the doubts, they're basically powers that you buy at a fixed XP cost and have Obtenebration + Occult as prerequisites.<br /> <br /> V5 doesn't really gives you the same vibe as the original Abyss Mysticism, but that's neither good or bad. Abyss Mysticism was really weird, so not always the best mechanic for what it was supposed to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I strongly prefer that DAV20 optional rule I mentioned. There's just no goofball workarounds or rules quibbles, Abyss Mysticism just is your form of blood sorcery, Obtenebration is your primary path, and you learn everything else following default blood sorcery rules. <i>Slightly</i> overpowered perhaps, but simple, and easy to understand and adjudicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T18:35:00-07:00","id":1541825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1541727-v20-is-abyss-mysticism-mechanically-speaking-a-seperate-discipline?p=1541817#post1541817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I strongly prefer that DAV20 optional rule I mentioned. There's just no goofball workarounds or rules quibbles, Abyss Mysticism just is your form of blood sorcery, Obtenebration is your primary path, and you learn everything else following default blood sorcery rules. <i>Slightly</i> overpowered perhaps, but simple, and easy to understand and adjudicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's overpowered. Are the actual rituals still the same? If yes, then I'd say it's pretty ok. AM rituals are strong, but their flaws are stingy, I personally never had a PC that really could afford more than two of them and still be playable. I won't remember all of them as it has been a long time since I looked them, but I distinctly remember their downsides being quite prohibitive.<br /> <br /> And if it is just access to rituals in general, I don't think any particular Discipline becoming Blood Sorcery would be too much of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}